clusion:**\nThe move at **K8** is the best choice. It creates a lethal threat (mate-in-1 at J8) that forces a specific response from White, while simultaneously blocking White\'s potential offensive expansion along the I6-J7 diagonal.\n\nEvaluation: The move K8 is a dual-purpose move that acts as a lethal threat and a prophylactic block. It forces White to fill J8, neutralizing Black\'s immediate threat but leaving White without a counter-threat and preventing White from connecting I6-J7-K8.\n\nReason: K8 creates a 4-stone trap on row 8 (G8-H8-I8- -K8) where playing J8 would form 5-in-a-row. White is forced to play J8 to block. Simultaneously, playing K8 blocks White from extending their diagonal (I6-J7) to K8, which would have created a dangerous open-3 for White.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "K", "row": 8}'}
